My good lord,

The council sat this morning touching the lead and bells of Glastonbury Abbey=
. Opinions were divided, but the King's will carried the day.

I trust this note finds you all in one piece.

In haste,
King Henry VIII

--
Sent from my writing-desk. Pray excuse any brevity or blots.
